<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 4.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 4.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on October 3. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		    P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1  Portman Min	     290.48    1.83</p>
<p>2  Niugini Min	     270.50    3.76</p>
<p>3  Mayne Nickless	  200.45    8.86</p>
<p>4  T N T		     172.66    2.40</p>
<p>5  Adel Bton Cement	123.91    1.71</p>
<p>6  Colonial Coml	   118.03    2.16</p>
<p>7  Herald Rsc		 91.15    1.03</p>
<p>8  Forrestania Gold	 85.32    2.15</p>
<p>9  Westral Forest	   76.09    2.10</p>
<p>10 Cape Range		 72.97    0.27</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1  Dominion Min		2.81    0.68</p>
<p>2  Computer Power	    3.42    3.50</p>
<p>3  Premier Inv		 3.49    0.62</p>
<p>4  BTR Plc		    5.37    0.70</p>
<p>5  Parbury Ltd		 5.96    5.45</p>
